1. PROJECT OVERVIEW.

This report documents the reconnaissance and initial vulnerabilty scanning performed against Kioptrix vulnerable virtual machine.

The assessment was conducted using Kali Linux within a VirtualBox lab environment.

The objective was to discover the target, identify active network services examine exposed ports and investigate potential web server vulnerabilities.



2. LAB ENVIRONMENT

Component                                   Details  

Attacker Machine                           Kali Linux

Target Machine                             Kioptrix

Target IP Address                          10.0.2.6

Target MAC Address                         08:00:27:6D:BF:4A

Network Discovery Tool                     Netdiscover

Port Scanning Tool                         Nmap


3. HOST DISCOVERY USING NETDISCOVER

Objective

Identify active devives within the network and locale the kioptrix target

Command : sudo netdiscover -r 10.0.2.0/24             

Observations 

Netdiscover identified two hosts on the network:

IP Address                                MAC Address

10.0.2.2                                 08:00:27:0A:DE

10.0.2.6                                 08:00:27:6D:BF:4A

The target selected for further investigation was:

10.0.2.6

The MAC address was identified as an oracle VirtualBox virtual network adapter.

Conclusion:

Host discovery successfully identified the kioptrix machine and established its IP and MAC address for subsequent scanning.

4. INITIAL NMAP PORT SCANNING

Objective :

Identify open TCP ports and determine which network services were accessible on the target.

Command : nmap 10.0.2.6

The most default Nmap scan checks the most common TCP ports.

Scan Results:

The target was confirmed to be online.

Nmap reported:

-Host status Up

-Latency 0.0018 seconds

-Closed TCP ports: 994.


Open Ports Identified

Port                       State                    Service

22/tcp                     Open                       SSH

80/tcp                     Open                       HTTP

111/tcp                    Open                      RPCBind

139/tcp                    Open                     NetBIOS-SSN

443/tcp                    Open                      HTTPS

32768/tcp                  Open                     FileNet-TMS

Nmap identified the vendor as:

Oracle virtualBox virtual NIC.

Obversations:

The scan identified six open TCP Ports.

The exposed services indicated that the target was running remote access, web RPC and SMB-related services.

These services were selected for further investigation.

5. WEB SERVER VULNERABILTY SCANNING - NIKTO

Objective

Investigate the web server running on the target and identify potentially insecure configurations and known vulnerability signatures.

Command : nikto -h 10.0.2.6

Explanation:

nikto launches the Nikto web server scanner.

-h specifies the target host.

10.0.2.6 is the target IP address.

